-- title:
--   Node data at a supersingular place: centre, Igusa end, layers
-- statement:
--   **Standing data.** A prime $q$ and a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, which by [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16) means that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; the inclusion `hle` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-function fields $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the first being the Laurent base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$, the second the base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\bigr)$; a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, and the compatibilities recorded in that structure), together with the hypothesis `hR₀` that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ this image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s\in W$.
--
--   **Constants frame.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; and `hκ`, that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime data.** A prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Layer family.** A type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_l$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_l$ of $K_l$ with $A_l=A\cap K_l$; an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_l$ for all $l$; and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in the image of some $K_l$.
--
--   **Tame uniformiser.** An element $\pi_t\in A$ with $\pi_t^{q^2-1}=q$, and `htame`: every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with $A.\mathrm{tameCharacter}\,\pi_t\,\tau=1$ fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise.
--
--   **Base layer.** The intermediate field $K_b=\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with $A_b=A\cap K_b$, and a generator $\varpi_b\neq 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Quantified objects.** With $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ made a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: (i) $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; (ii) the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is everything; (iii) $F_0$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta:\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (iv) linear disjointness: for $K'$ finite over $k_0$, for $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   Further: every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$; every subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure; the hypotheses `hjR` that $j$ (the class of the $q$-expansion `jq`) lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, `hjs` that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and `hJK` that `jqNModC` of level $q$ lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; an element $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue satisfies $\bar a_0^{\,q}=s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$; and a finset `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$.
--
--   **The model hypothesis.** These are assumed to satisfy one long conjunction, grouped as follows and summarised here. (M1) *$W_0$ is the arithmetic model at $s$*: $x\in k_0$ maps into $W_0$ exactly when $x\in A$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with $\pi_0$ as uniformiser; for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, has no pole where $j$ has none (expressed by $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of $j$ implying $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of $g$ for all places $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$ to any constant $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue; and $W_0$ is stable under the operators $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. (M2) *$B$ is a chart for $W_0$*: $A_b\to B$ is compatible with the inclusions into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; $B$ lies in the compositum of $F_0$ with the constants from $K_b$ and has that compositum as fraction field; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$ and $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $B$ lies in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$ and $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from it; $j\in B$ and $B$ is stable under the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ operators for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; $B$ contains an element cutting out the non-affine locus (an element avoiding every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and in which $j$ is residually transcendental), and, for each supersingular place $s'\neq s$, an element of $B$ avoiding every $V$ realising the reduction conditions at $s'$; and, for each $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ making `CoordRing` a domain and each $\zeta$, a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of order $2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ and a ring map $\rho$ from $B$ to the corresponding Drinfeld quotient field with kernel $(\varpi_b)$, compatible with the reduction of $A_b$, with fraction field the target, with image exactly the image of `CoordRing`, and intertwining $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ with the action `hFunctionFieldAction` of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$. (M3) *`nodes` is the set of node rings*: $\#\,\mathrm{nodes}=q+1$; there is a common chart $B_c$, generated by the constants $k_0\cap A$ and a finite set, contained in every $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$, each $O$ being the localisation of $B_c$ at its units; the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ operators permute `nodes`, and act transitively on it; distinct nodes are separated (there is a common element, a non-unit of one and a unit of the other); and every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the reduction conditions at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates some node. (M4) *per-node structure*, for every $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is local and noetherian; $x\in k_0$ maps into $O$ exactly when $x\in A$; every element of $O$ is congruent to a constant from $k_0\cap A$ modulo non-units; and there are an exponent $E_0\ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for a unit $v$ of $A$ lying in $k_0$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, $\iota$ carries constants to `const`, $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and $c_x$ does not; the Igusa germ clause: `jqNModC` minus $a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and its image under $\iota$ is a unit times $V^e$ with $e\ge 1$; a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, inducing $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\pi_0$, admitting a residually transcendental element, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, reading the modular functions $g$ as above (the $W_x$-valuation of the image of $g$ is positive exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ the image lies in $O$ and is a non-unit away from the matching constant), and separating $O$ from the other nodes; and a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B\cap O$, whose elements have no poles where $j$ has none, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, with $F_0$ as fraction field, generated by the constants $k_0\cap A$ and a finite set, and containing an element avoiding every valuation subring $V$ (subject to the usual constant, $\pi_0$ and residual-transcendence conditions) that fails to contain $O$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above, for every field $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ and every `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $F_{ss}$ with $R.\mathrm{integers}\cap F_0=W_0$; for every $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$; for every $E_0\ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$, $v,v^{-1}\in A$, $v\in k_0$; and for every layerwise completion datum, consisting of subrings $C'_l$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$, each a discrete valuation domain with a chosen element $\varpi'_l$, types $W_l$ which are adically complete discrete valuation domains with elements $\pi_l$, exponents $e_l$ and ring maps $j_l:C'_l\to W_l$, subject to: $C'_l=A\cap K_l$; the residue of $d\in C'_l$ in $A$ vanishes exactly when $\varpi'_l\mid d$; $C'_{n_0}\le C'_l$; $\pi_l$ irreducible; $\pi_0=v\,(\varpi'_l)^{e_l}$ with $v,v^{-1}\in C'_l$; $j_l(\varpi'_l)=\pi_l$; $j_l$ reflects divisibility by powers of $\pi_l$; and $j_l$ has dense image (every $w\in W_l$ is congruent to some $j_l(c)$ modulo $\pi_l^n$) — there exist a place $nd$ of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$, a field $FI$ over that residue field, a `RegularProlongation` $R_x$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $FI$, a place $b_x$ of $FI$, a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$, a set $S$ of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a subring $\mathcal N$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, subrings $\mathcal N_0(l)$ which are local and noetherian, and elements $c_x,c_y,c_u$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   1. $nd$ is rational, that is, the residue field of $nd$ is generated by the residue field of $A$.
--
--   2. $R_x.\mathrm{integers}\cap F_0=W_x$.
--
--   3. $O\subseteq W_x$, and $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$.
--
--   4. *Canonicity of the Igusa branch*: there is $c_{yO}\in O$ whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is $c_y$, which is not in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, and which characterises $W_x$ as the smallest such branch: any valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and $c_{yO}$ outside it, contains $W_x$.
--
--   5. *The two-node half-unit*: for every $O'\in\mathrm{nodes}$ with $O'\neq O$ there is $g\in O\cap O'$ of the form $g=c\cdot u$ with $c\in O$ mapping to $c_x$ and $u$ a unit of $O$, such that $g$ is a unit of $O'$.
--
--   6. *Centre and place set*: $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$; $O$ maps into $\mathcal N_0(n_0)$ and non-units of $O$ remain non-units there; a place $P$ lies in $S$ exactly when $O$ lies in its valuation subring and, for every non-unit $f$ of $O$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; the $R$-residues of elements of $O$ lie in the valuation subring of $nd$, those of non-units of $O$ lie in its maximal ideal; and $nd$ is the unique place of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ with these two properties.
--
--   7. $b_x$, $nd$ and every $P\in S$ are rational.
--
--   8. $f\in\mathcal N$ exactly when $f$ lies in $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$, in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P\in S$; and for $f\in\mathcal N$ and $P\in S$ one has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$.
--
--   9. *Node modulus*: $c_x c_y=(\varpi'_{n_0})^{e_{n_0}E_0}\cdot c_u$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$.
--
--   10. *Branch readings*: $R_x$ kills $c_x$; $nd.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $c_x$ equals $1$; $R$ kills $c_y$; $b_x.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R_x$-residue of $c_y$ equals $1$.
--
--   11. *Tame equivariance*: for every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ with $A.\mathrm{tameCharacter}\,\pi_t\,\tau=1$, writing $g$ for $\mathrm{arithmeticGalois}$ of $\tau$ on the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, the set $S$ satisfies $P\in S\iff g\cdot P\in S$, and $g$ fixes $c_x$ and $c_y$.
--
--   12. Every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is a quotient of elements of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ for some $l$; and for every $f$ there are $n$, constants $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$, elements $a_i$ and a non-zero $b$ of $\mathcal N_0(n_0)$ with $f\,b=\sum_i c_i\,a_i$.
--
--   13. *Layered node rings*: for every $l$, $\mathcal N_0(n_0)\le\mathcal N_0(l)\le\mathcal N$; $P\in S$ exactly when $\mathcal N_0(l)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ in the maximal ideal of $A$; $C'_l$ maps into $\mathcal N_0(l)$; every element of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ differs from a constant of $C'_l$ by a non-unit; constants linearly independent over $C'_l$ admit no non-trivial relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ with $a_i\in\mathcal N_0(l)$; there is a subring $B_x$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ inside $\mathcal N_0(l)$, containing $c_x$, $c_y$ and $c_u$, with $\mathcal N_0(l)$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, and generated by the constants from $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal N_0(l)$ and $c_u$ is a unit of $\mathcal N_0(l)$; and there are a ring map $\sigma$ from $W_l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0(l)$ and an isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W_l\,(\pi_l^{\,e_lE_0})$ such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota_c\circ\sigma=\mathrm{const}$, the element `jqNModC` minus $a_0$ lies in $\mathcal N_0(l)$ with $\iota_c$-image a unit times $V^e$ for some $e\ge 1$, every constant of $C'_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and the two crossing readings hold: if $f\in\mathcal N_0(l)$ has non-zero $R_x$-residue of $b_x$-order $n$, then $\iota_c(f)-\gamma V^n$ lies in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\pi_l)$ and $U$ for some unit $\gamma$; if $f$ has non-zero $R$-residue of $nd$-order $n$, then $\iota_c(f)-\gamma U^n$ lies in the ideal generated by $\mathrm{const}(\pi_l)$ and $V$ for some unit $\gamma$.
--
--   14. *Centre reading*: for $P\in S$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with no pole where $j$ has none and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   15. *Igusa-side end over $s$*: every element of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ maps into $R_x.\mathrm{integers}$, and there is a ring map $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to $FI$ such that the $R_x$-residue of the image of any $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ is $j$ applied to its $R_0$-residue, and such that $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ exactly when $j(g)$ lies in that of $b_x$.
--
--   The statement is the version valid for every prime $q$; no lower bound on $q$ beyond primality is assumed.
--
--   This is the per-node step in the description of the special fibre at $q$ of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of reduction to level $q$: for one node $O$ of the supersingular fibre it produces the node's centre place, the canonical Igusa-side branch together with a regular prolongation and a place tracing it, the layered local node rings with their Tate-style $uv=\pi^{e}$ crossing presentations, and the node coordinates $c_x,c_y,c_u$ with their readings on the two branches. It is used by the $k$-level node-core assembly [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
